Vendored third-party components — VpncBar for Windows
=====================================================

VpncBar bundles three third-party components, each redistributed under its own
license. Full source for the GPL/LGPL pieces is either included here
(vendor/vpnc) or available from the upstream URLs and the pinned versions
below. This file mirrors the provenance discipline of the macOS VpncBar repo.


vendor/vpnc/  — vpnc (Cisco IPSec client), Windows-ported
---------------------------------------------------------
Upstream base : https://github.com/streambinder/vpnc   (a maintained fork of
                vpnc 0.5.3, originally by Maurice Massar et al.)
utun port from: https://github.com/breiter/vpnc        (0.5.3-xnu, by Brian Reiter)
License       : GPL v2 or later (see vendor/vpnc/LICENSE). Includes cisco-decrypt.

The full, modified source is in this repository (vendor/vpnc/src). VpncBar
builds it from source — there is no separate binary distribution to offer.

Local modifications for Windows (on top of the macOS utun port this fork
already carries). All are guarded by `#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__CYGWIN__)`
so the macOS/Unix paths are untouched:

  src/sysdep-win.c        (new)
    - Wintun tunnel backend: loads wintun.dll from the executable's directory
      (the signed driver from wintun.net), creates an adapter, and implements
      tun_open/tun_close/tun_read/tun_write over a Wintun session — the Windows
      analog of this tree's native-utun port. Exports the adapter index as
      $TUNIDX for the config script (as openconnect does on Windows).
    - A dedicated reader thread pumps the (non-selectable) tunnel device, the
      strategy the in-tree Cygwin port established.
    - Graceful-stop watcher: waits on a named event (VPNCBAR_STOP_EVENT, set by
      the VpncBar service) and a console-ctrl handler, setting do_kill — the
      SIGTERM analog. A loopback "self-pipe" interrupts select() promptly.
    - syslog/openlog shims (output to stderr, captured by the service), setenv/
      unsetenv/error/uname/inet_aton shims, a CreateProcess-based system()
      (no cmd.exe quote mangling), and a close() that handles winsock SOCKETs.
    - winsock is initialized from a constructor (upstream main() untouched).

  src/sysdep-win32.h, src/win32/*  (new)
    - Compatibility header (winsock2 + small POSIX shims, WSAPoll for poll(),
      WIFEXITED/WEXITSTATUS, a BSD `struct ip`, etc.) plus a directory of stub
      headers that route the upstream BSD #includes to it.

  src/tunip.c
    - vpnc_main_loop(): the socket side stays in select(); the tunnel device is
      pumped by a Win32 thread (mirrors the existing Cygwin #ifdef path). A
      loopback wake socket lets a stop request interrupt select() at once.
    - vpnc_doit(): no fork()/daemonize and no POSIX signals on Windows — the
      service keeps vpnc as a foreground child; the stop watcher replaces the
      signal handlers.

  src/vpnc.c
    - The IKE socket write() becomes send() on Windows (winsock SOCKETs are not
      CRT fds). The config script runs via CreateProcess (win32_system).

  src/config.c
    - The interactive password prompt (termios echo toggling) and the external
      password-helper (fork/exec/pipe) are compiled out on Windows; VpncBar
      always feeds the full config — including secrets — on stdin, so neither
      path is reachable.

  src/Makefile.win32  (new)
    - mingw-w64 build: links libgcrypt + GnuTLS (certificate support enabled —
      a feature upgrade over the macOS default CRYPTO_NONE build), plus
      ws2_32 and iphlpapi. Built by scripts/build-vpnc.ps1.

  The macOS `--log-file` option is retained but unused on Windows: the service
  captures vpnc's stdout/stderr directly (no daemonization), so the per-profile
  session log is produced the same way for both backends.


vendor/openconnect/  — openconnect (Cisco AnyConnect SSL client)
----------------------------------------------------------------
Upstream : https://www.infradead.org/openconnect/
Version  : openconnect 9.12 — the exact source tarball
           (openconnect-9.12.tar.gz) is downloaded from the upstream URL above,
           pinned to that version, by scripts/build-openconnect.ps1 at build
           time (it is not committed to this repo; for a binary release, attach
           that tarball as the corresponding LGPL source).
License  : LGPL v2.1 (see the COPYING.LGPL inside the tarball).

Built from that source with mingw-w64 (scripts/build-openconnect.ps1), unmodified
except for the build flags recorded in that script (a -Wno-incompatible-pointer-
types relaxation for GCC 14, and wintun.h supplied from vendor/wintun). Shipped
as a separate executable, so the LGPL relinking right is satisfied; the exact
dependency package versions are recorded in vendor/openconnect/VERSIONS.txt.

Bundled dependency DLLs (the mingw-w64 closure of openconnect.exe and, shared,
of vpnc.exe). Each is redistributed under its own license; all are
GPL-compatible:

  libgnutls-30          GnuTLS              LGPL v2.1+
  libnettle-8,
  libhogweed-6          Nettle              LGPL v3+ / GPL v2+ (dual)
  libgmp-10             GMP                 LGPL v3+ / GPL v2+ (dual)
  libtasn1-6            libtasn1            LGPL v2.1+
  libp11-kit-0          p11-kit             BSD-3-Clause
  libidn2-0             libidn2             LGPL v3+ / GPL v2+
  libunistring-5        libunistring        LGPL v3+
  libxml2-16            libxml2             MIT
  libzstd, libzstd.dll  Zstandard           BSD-3-Clause / GPL v2 (dual)
  zlib1                 zlib                zlib license
  libbrotli{common,dec,enc}  Brotli         MIT
  libffi-8              libffi              MIT
  libiconv-2, libintl-8 GNU libiconv/gettext LGPL v2.1+
  libgcrypt-20          libgcrypt           LGPL v2.1+
  libgpg-error-0        libgpg-error        LGPL v2.1+
  libwinpthread-1       mingw-w64 winpthreads  ZPL / MIT (see mingw-w64)

Source for any of these is obtainable from the MSYS2 mingw64 repository at the
versions in vendor/openconnect/VERSIONS.txt, or from each project upstream.


vendor/wintun/  — Wintun (TUN driver), prebuilt
-----------------------------------------------
Upstream : https://www.wintun.net/
Version  : 0.14.1 (wintun.dll, per-arch, fetched by scripts/fetch-wintun.ps1;
           not committed to this repo)
License  : WireGuard LLC "Prebuilt Binaries License" (vendor/wintun/LICENSE.txt),
           which permits redistribution as part of a larger product. The Wintun
           source itself is GPL v2; we ship the signed prebuilt dll as intended
           by upstream (we cannot sign a kernel driver ourselves).

The same wintun.dll is used by both backends (openconnect >= 8.10 loads it from
its own directory; our vpnc port loads it from the executable's directory).


VpncBar application
-------------------
The VpncBar application code (src/VpncBar) is covered by this repository's
LICENSE. It links no GPL code — it launches the GPL/LGPL backends as separate
processes — so its own licensing is independent of the vendored components.
